        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                "word": "énormité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "bfbf3778-4033-44c7-89bc-79a66b7081a0",
                        "entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "énormités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "259af893-fb8c-3c47-b34f-b65ca0577b83",
                        "entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualité de ce qui est énorme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e445fd3-c2b1-42a1-a9a3-13d08655543d",
                                "sense_id": "259af893-fb8c-3c47-b34f-b65ca0577b83",
                                "text": "On conçoit aisément l’énormité de la tâche si l'on songe au nombre de populations qui ont pu depuis le Néogène être progressivement insularisées chorologiquement et surtout écologiquement autour de la Méditerranée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad592bc7-dcbb-412a-9c33-36c674a255a8",
                                "sense_id": "259af893-fb8c-3c47-b34f-b65ca0577b83",
                                "text": "Tentons de saisir l’énormité des distances impliquées. Il y a environ 200 milliards d’étoiles dans notre galaxie qui a un diamètre de 100 000 années-lumière."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a0f5325-c232-3a74-82ca-e8e73dd64366",
                        "entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Gravité, atrocité, en parlant de crimes, de méfaits."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fd60229-3fc8-486c-aeff-af6fcada38a4",
                                "sense_id": "8a0f5325-c232-3a74-82ca-e8e73dd64366",
                                "text": "L’énormité des abus et le besoin d’une grande réforme le frappaient; mais, se défiant de son inexpérience, et indécis par caractère, il hésitait."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc5cf746-4bf7-3150-a7d9-8f0b9c800411",
                        "entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Actions honteuses ou atroces."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40adb238-e9c4-4a93-b172-6f0ae323c202",
                                "sense_id": "cc5cf746-4bf7-3150-a7d9-8f0b9c800411",
                                "text": "Commettre des énormités."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8de1c07e-5c99-3418-b17a-8373b47450ec",
                        "entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Opinions, paroles absurdes, extravagantes, odieuses, révoltantes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "69db8c22-ba9f-4f1b-9a94-cf13f7f2b54f",
                                "sense_id": "8de1c07e-5c99-3418-b17a-8373b47450ec",
                                "text": "Deux ou trois médecins s’exclamèrent. Les autres semblaient hésiter. Quant au préfet, il sursauta et se retourna machinalement vers la porte, comme pour vérifier qu’elle avait bien empêché cette énormité de se répandre dans les couloirs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "927c9835-3a51-41c9-bc64-0a08331e7c57",
                                "sense_id": "8de1c07e-5c99-3418-b17a-8373b47450ec",
                                "text": "Dans un petit ouvrage écrit sur moi, j’apprends avec intérêt que je viens de la Nouvelle-Angleterre, ce qui expliquerait ma « conscience puritaine ». Mais ma famille ne vient pas de la Nouvelle-Angleterre et je ne crois pas avoir dans les veines une seule goutte de sang puritain. Mes parents venaient des États du Sud. Si l’on parle ainsi des écrivains vivants, quelles énormités n’écrit-on pas sur les morts ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1fbfc47-e434-46b7-a197-76ae828a423a",
                                "sense_id": "8de1c07e-5c99-3418-b17a-8373b47450ec",
                                "text": "Mitch pouvait continuer à proférer des énormités à son égard, elle comptait se conformer à son plan jusqu’à ce que les deux rejetons Kincaid deviennent proches."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91196ca8-b20b-49d5-999a-17923cbf2f60",
                        "source_entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "target_lang_word": "enormousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "enormousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a496c87-c349-3c91-b9ff-a0bc2b9238ec",
                                        "entry_id": "36e17952-b4c9-3bda-9bf1-013ab0aa1576",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Great size or magnitude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abc2b5c9-68a7-421e-9219-b767567d8c0f",
                                                "sense_id": "6a496c87-c349-3c91-b9ff-a0bc2b9238ec",
                                                "text": "\"The Last Emperor,\" written by Mark Peploe \"with\" (as the credits say) Mr. Bertolucci, may have been inhibited by the enormousness of its subject, and even by the apparently enthusiastic support of China, which acted as host to Mr. Bertolucci, his cast and production crew."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf3ee2fe-0290-4566-b0a3-1ea88da38627",
                                                "sense_id": "6a496c87-c349-3c91-b9ff-a0bc2b9238ec",
                                                "text": "I stood close to heartsick mourners and worried that I would not sustain the enormousness of their spiritual weight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "030d86d3-713c-4fe1-b5df-c62cf3c8c979",
                        "source_entry_id": "a031e6df-ca4c-3f0b-ab37-b4b8c1be0828",
                        "target_lang_word": "enormity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "enormity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8414cfca-2800-3787-87d8-76142be771a4",
                                        "entry_id": "3b5c64b8-c88e-3c87-98e6-b425a7134dc6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deviation from what is normal or standard; irregularity, abnormality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8e0f451-6544-3802-92bb-0a09f79e1737",
                                        "entry_id": "3b5c64b8-c88e-3c87-98e6-b425a7134dc6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deviation from moral normality; extreme wickedness, nefariousness, or cruelty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22337de5-c1bc-4b6d-a606-76750e3619a5",
                                                "sense_id": "b8e0f451-6544-3802-92bb-0a09f79e1737",
                                                "text": "Not until the war ended and journalists were able to enter Cambodia did the world really become aware of the enormity of Pol Pot’s oppression."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cde84b84-3d4b-4071-8c65-904ff3b9d896",
                                                "sense_id": "b8e0f451-6544-3802-92bb-0a09f79e1737",
                                                "text": "I had an obscure feeling that all was not over, and that he would still commit some signal crime, which by its enormity should almost efface the recollection of the past."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb1c9feb-929c-4d74-b0d4-940e5ddb2f72",
                                                "sense_id": "b8e0f451-6544-3802-92bb-0a09f79e1737",
                                                "text": "Hannah Arendt coined the phrase \"the banality of evil\" in her dispatches for The New Yorker from Adolf Eichmann's trial in Jerusalem in 1961. It was her attempt to square the mediocrity of the man with the enormity of his crimes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf81a620-586f-36d9-a8b3-e5f07f2fa357",
                                        "entry_id": "3b5c64b8-c88e-3c87-98e6-b425a7134dc6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A breach of law or morality; a transgression, an act of evil or wickedness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a025d625-a806-40d3-b076-03655fa6f4bf",
                                                "sense_id": "cf81a620-586f-36d9-a8b3-e5f07f2fa357",
                                                "text": "Yet she appeared confident in innocence, and did not tremble, although gazed on and execrated by thousands; for all the kindness which her beauty might otherwise have excited, was obliterated in the minds of the spectators by the imagination of the enormity she was supposed to have committed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c0be035-1ba0-43c4-8bf2-3f04bae646bf",
                                                "sense_id": "cf81a620-586f-36d9-a8b3-e5f07f2fa357",
                                                "text": "Monsters of impurity, avaricious wretches, poisoners, have occupied the papal see. A learned bishop (Maret of the General Council) expresses himself with holy indignation in reference to the frightful enormities of the tenth century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05e0402b-c464-4893-85ae-8a2ad96b05f8",
                                                "sense_id": "cf81a620-586f-36d9-a8b3-e5f07f2fa357",
                                                "text": "In 1650 Lieutenant William Jackson was in trouble for holding, among many other enormities, ‘community of all things’, including, apparently, wives."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2bbcb825-f773-31c5-82f3-b113f71962cb",
                                        "entry_id": "3b5c64b8-c88e-3c87-98e6-b425a7134dc6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Great size; enormousness, hugeness, immenseness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "beacd572-dc7f-4666-9491-82df2116a07d",
                                                "sense_id": "2bbcb825-f773-31c5-82f3-b113f71962cb",
                                                "text": "I am in Amerika! I felt like weeping at the enormity of this fact. Amerika, the fabled, the mythic, the coveted. The knowledge that we had no visas, and therefore would not be allowed to set foot on land, dampened my enthusiasm only a little."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48a8752d-64f6-4d74-92da-2ba3787289c2",
                                                "sense_id": "2bbcb825-f773-31c5-82f3-b113f71962cb",
                                                "text": "But the enormity of Clement's vision of papal grandeur only became clear once the public rooms were completed during the years that immediately followed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6865795c-4570-4d85-bb04-27c24d4fbbb7",
                                                "sense_id": "2bbcb825-f773-31c5-82f3-b113f71962cb",
                                                "text": "[Wayne] Rooney and his team-mates started ponderously, as if sensing the enormity of the occasion, but once [Paul] Scholes began to link with Ryan Giggs in the middle of the park, the visitors increased the tempo with Sunderland struggling to keep up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "718ee5e7-ff57-4e95-904b-c4f1623e053d",
